Part 1: Determine a Topic
Step 1: Ask a question
Chosen topic: Internet usage in South Africa.

1. Research question

How has internet usage in South Africa changed over the past 10 years?

Benefit of answering this question:

The analysis will help us understand how internet access and usage have changed in South Africa. It can show whether more people are using the internet and help identify the importance of technology in education, communication and business. The findings could also help identify the need for improved internet access in rural communities.

2. Type of data analysis

Descriptive analysis.

Reason: Descriptive analysis is suitable because the project will use historical data to identify trends and changes in internet usage over a 10-year period.
Step 2: Determine the Data Needed
1. List of data elements required

The following data will be needed to answer the research question:
1. Year of data collection (2015–2024).
2. Percentage of South African population using the internet each year.
3. Number of internet users in South Africa.
4. Mobile internet usage.
5. Availability of internet access in urban and rural areas.
6. Access to broadband and mobile networks.
2. Search for data elements

I would use internet search engines to find historical internet usage statistics for South Africa.

3. Sources of data identified

The following websites provide useful information and open datasets:
Source	Information available
World Bank Open Data	Historical internet usage statistics
International Telecommunication Union (ITU)	Global internet and telecommunications statistics
Statistics South Africa	Household access to internet and ICT statistics
Kaggle	Sample datasets for data analysis

