1. Why is it important to identify the question that needs to be answered by the analysis before beginning the project?

It is important to identify the question before starting because it gives direction to the project. It helps the analyst understand what information is needed, which data sources to use and what type of analysis should be performed. It also prevents wasting time collecting unnecessary information and ensures that the results answer the original question.

